control: A process starts in order, refusing the password variables before it reads its configuration, logging every value before it sets the level, and running the configuration's checks before Init
removes: the password variables are refused after the configuration is read, so a start whose configuration cannot be read reports that error instead
packages: ./process
tests: TestThePasswordVariablesAreRefusedBeforeTheConfigurationIsRead/until_stopped/PGPASSWORD=secret TestThePasswordVariablesAreRefusedBeforeTheConfigurationIsRead/until_stopped/PGPASSWORD= TestThePasswordVariablesAreRefusedBeforeTheConfigurationIsRead/until_stopped/PGSSLPASSWORD=secret TestThePasswordVariablesAreRefusedBeforeTheConfigurationIsRead/until_stopped/PGSSLPASSWORD= TestThePasswordVariablesAreRefusedBeforeTheConfigurationIsRead/once/PGPASSWORD=secret TestThePasswordVariablesAreRefusedBeforeTheConfigurationIsRead/once/PGPASSWORD= TestThePasswordVariablesAreRefusedBeforeTheConfigurationIsRead/once/PGSSLPASSWORD=secret TestThePasswordVariablesAreRefusedBeforeTheConfigurationIsRead/once/PGSSLPASSWORD=
scheduled-count: no

